1
00:05:10,909 --> 00:05:16,909
A man called "Horse" becomes an Indian warrior in the
most electrifying ritual ever seen!

2
00:10:21,818 --> 00:10:27,818
A Man Called Horse is a western, drama film directed by Elliot Silverstein.

3
00:15:32,727 --> 00:15:38,727
In 1825, English peer Lord John Morgan is cast adrift in the American West.

4
00:20:43,636 --> 00:20:49,636
Captured by Sioux Indians, Morgan is at first targeted for quick
extinction, but the tribesmen sense that he is worthy of survival.

5
00:25:54,545 --> 00:26:00,545
He eventually passes the many necessary tests that will
permit him to become a member of the tribe.

6
00:31:05,454 --> 00:31:11,454
John Morgan, played by Richard Harris.

7
00:36:16,363 --> 00:36:22,363
Batise, played by Jean Gascon.

8
00:41:27,272 --> 00:41:33,272
Buffalo Cow Head, played by Judith Anderson.

9
00:46:38,181 --> 00:46:44,181
Running Deer, played by Corinna Tsopei.

10
00:51:49,090 --> 00:51:55,090
Yellow Hand, played by Manu Tupou.

11
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Joe, played by Dub Taylor.

12
01:02:10,909 --> 01:02:16,909
A Man Called Horse is a 1970 Western film directed by Elliot
Silverstein, produced by Sandy Howard, and written by Jack DeWitt.

13
01:07:21,818 --> 01:07:27,818
It is based on a short story of the same name by the Western writer Dorothy M.

14
01:12:32,727 --> 01:12:38,727
Johnson, first published in 1950 in Collier's magazine and
again in 1968 in Johnson's book Indian Country.

15
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
The basic story was used in a 1958 episode of the television
series Wagon Train, also titled "A Man Called Horse".

16
01:22:54,545 --> 01:23:00,545
The film stars Richard Harris as the titular character, alongside Judith Anderson,
Jean Gascon, Manu Tupou, Corinna Tsopei, Dub Taylor, and James Gammon.

17
01:28:05,454 --> 01:28:11,454
Partially spoken in Sioux, the film tells the story of an English
aristocrat who is captured by the Sioux people.

18
01:33:16,363 --> 01:33:22,363
The film was a Mexican-American co-production filmed on location in
Arizona and the Mexican states of Durango and Sonora.

19
01:38:27,272 --> 01:38:33,272
It received generally positive critical reviews, and was a financial success, spawning two sequels;
The Return of a Man Called Horse (1976) and Triumphs of a Man Called Horse (1983).

20
01:43:38,181 --> 01:43:44,181
The film explores themes of ambush, ritual, indian
territory, native american, aristocrat.

21
01:48:49,090 --> 01:48:55,090
The tone is emotional.
